Hi Joshua,

I hope you are well.

IT RCSA has completed the 2026 testing of the five BSI SDLC key controls (BSI=
.IT.23.C1, C13, C17, C25 and C4) for the review period 09/01/2025 =E2=80=93 0=
8/31/2026, using the two sampled projects: ALCO =E2=80=93 Security Lending (D=
H 3263) and Derivatives Non-Deliverable Forwards =E2=80=93 NDF (DH 3264). Tha=
nk you and the team for the evidence provided so far.

Most of the testing passed. Before we finalize the results, we need your help=
 with 13 points: one failed sample and some confirmations / additional eviden=
ce. Each point is explained in the attached document with the exact document =
and a screenshot of what we are referring to.

SUMMARY BY CONTROL

1) BSI.IT.23.C1 Business Requirement =E2=80=93 Sample 1 (Security Lending) FA=
IL, Sample 2 (NDF) Pass
   =E2=80=A2 CR-01 (High): the Business Requirements for Release 01 (Appian) =
were approved by the Sponsor on 02/06/2026, after the Build gate (PTB) on 10/=
31/2025. The approval e-mail says "Those same documents were approved during =
phase 1". If you can provide the phase 1 BRD approval dated before 10/31/2025=
 that covers the Appian requirements, we can close the exception and C1 can s=
tay Satisfactory. Otherwise C1 will be rated Needs Improvement.

2) BSI.IT.23.C13 Design of System =E2=80=93 both samples Pass
   =E2=80=A2 CR-04: Enterprise Architecture approval was obtained as a Gate 5=
 item (12/04/2025 and 12/10/2025), after Build started. Was there an earlier =
EA / ARB review?
   =E2=80=A2 CR-05: NDF data risk is HIGH =E2=80=93 please provide the CDO da=
ta deliverables (data model / lineage) or the CDO confirmation.

3) BSI.IT.23.C17 Solution Intent Document =E2=80=93 both samples Pass
   =E2=80=A2 CR-06: the Security Lending Single Design shows Delivery Hub ID =
"1886 =E2=80=93 Securities Lending (JP Morgan)" and has no version dates =E2=
=80=93 please confirm it is the approved document for DH 3263.

4) BSI.IT.23.C25 Implement & Deployment =E2=80=93 both samples Pass
   =E2=80=A2 CR-07: in all 4 releases the final implementation plan was attac=
hed after the last approval and earlier versions were deleted (Security Lendi=
ng R01 held a "Cornercard" plan at approval time). Please confirm what change=
d and whether re-approval is required.
   =E2=80=A2 CR-08: the Roll Back section of the Security Lending R01 Deploym=
ent Plan is empty =E2=80=93 please confirm the rollback in the ticket is the =
approved plan.

5) BSI.IT.23.C4 Segregated Environments =E2=80=93 both samples Pass
   =E2=80=A2 CR-09: the same login (MIASANG) is used on production and non-pr=
oduction =E2=80=93 owner and access rights.
   =E2=80=A2 CR-10: non-production MIAAFT28 ("SANTANDER OCT 2025 EOM") holds =
client deals =E2=80=93 masking or Information Security approval.
   =E2=80=A2 CR-11: register of development / testing-in-production exception=
s with Information Security approval (or confirmation there were none).
   =E2=80=A2 CR-12: the evidence document was created on 10/22/2026, after th=
e period =E2=80=93 confirmation / dated evidence from the period.
   =E2=80=A2 CR-13: evidence of separate Appian DEV / TEST / PROD environment=
s.

6) All five controls
   =E2=80=A2 CR-02 (High): the ServiceNow list of releases deployed to produc=
tion in the period (with the query used), and why projects 3625 and 3512 have=
 a blank SDLC flag.
   =E2=80=A2 CR-03: approved version of the 2026 SDLC process map (it is stil=
l in Draft).

ATTACHED
   =E2=80=A2 SDLC2026 BSI - Clarification Request by Control.docx =E2=80=93 o=
ne document, one part per control. Each request shows what we found, the docu=
ments in question, screenshots with the exact place marked in red, what we ne=
ed, and a response page for your explanation.
   =E2=80=A2 SDLC2026 BSI - Clarification Tracker.xlsx =E2=80=93 the same 13 =
requests, one row each, to track the responses (yellow columns are for you).
   =E2=80=A2 SDLC2026 BSI Clarifications.zip =E2=80=93 copies of every docume=
nt in question and the screenshots, one folder per control and per request, w=
ith an empty "03 Your Response Evidence" folder where you can save new eviden=
ce. (Sent separately / shared via link because of its size =E2=80=93 17 MB.)

Some points may need input from other teams (Enterprise Architecture, CDO, In=
formation Security or the T24 / Appian teams). Please feel free to forward th=
e specific request and paste their answer in the document or tracker.

We would appreciate your response by 11/13/2026. Priority items are CR-01 and=
 CR-02, as they affect the C1 rating and the population. If it helps, I am ha=
ppy to set up a 30-minute call to walk through the points.

Thank you for your support.

Best regards,
Edward
